[{"category":"section","location":"library/#Library","page":"Library","text":"All functions exported by this package are listed below.","title":"Library"},{"category":"section","location":"library/#Library-Contents","page":"Library","text":"Pages = [\"library.md\"]\nDepth = 3","title":"Library Contents"},{"category":"section","location":"library/#Index","page":"Library","text":"","title":"Index"},{"category":"section","location":"library/#Functions","page":"Library","text":"","title":"Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"library/#Registry-Management","page":"Library","text":"","title":"Registry Management"},{"category":"section","location":"library/#Registry-Queries","page":"Library","text":"","title":"Registry Queries"},{"category":"section","location":"library/#Validations","page":"Library","text":"","title":"Validations"},{"category":"section","location":"library/#Conversions","page":"Library","text":"","title":"Conversions"},{"category":"section","location":"library/#IO","page":"Library","text":"","title":"IO"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.InitializeRegistry","page":"Library","text":"InitializeRegistry(; ID::T,\n                     Title::T = \"Example Project\",\n                     Authors::Dict{T, AuthorInfo} = Dict{String, AuthorInfo}(\"Author\" => AuthorInfo(Name=\"Author\")),\n                     Description::T = \"\") where {T <: AbstractString}\n\nInitialize a DataRegistry object with project metadata, but no datasets.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.InitializeRegistry"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.AddDataset!","page":"Library","text":"AddDataset!(registry::DataRegistry, dataset::Dataset)\n\nAdd dataset to a registry. Checks that the ID doesn't already exist, and that all the parent datasets exist.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.AddDataset!"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.UpdateDataset!","page":"Library","text":"UpdateDataset!(registry::DataRegistry, ID::String; kwargs...)\n\nUpdate fields of existing Dataset ID in registry. Only fields provided as keyword arguments are modified. Checks that the dataset exists, and that all provided fields are valid. The dataset's LastModified timestamp is updated automatically.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.UpdateDataset!"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.UpdateOrAddDataset!","page":"Library","text":"UpdateOrAddDataset!(registry::DataRegistry, ID::String; kwargs...)\n\nUpdate existing, or add new Dataset ID to registry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.UpdateOrAddDataset!"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.RemoveDataset!","page":"Library","text":"RemoveDataset!(registry::DataRegistry, ID; confirm=true, allow_orphans=true)\n\nRemove Dataset ID from registry. Checks that the dataset exists. Asks for confirmation if the dataset is a parent of any other datasets.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.RemoveDataset!"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.FindChildren","page":"Library","text":"FindChildren(registry::DataRegistry, ID::String)\n\nFind all Datasets in registry that have ID as a parent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.FindChildren"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.ValidateParents","page":"Library","text":"ValidateParents(registry::DataRegistry, Parents::Vector{String})\n\nVerfy that all Parents exist in the registry.\n\n\n\n\n\nValidateParents(registry::DataRegistry, Parent::String)\n\nVerfy that Parent exists in the registry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.ValidateParents"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.DataExists","page":"Library","text":"DataExists(DataPath::AbstractString)\n\nCheck if the data pointed to by DataPath exists on disk.\n\n\n\n\n\nDataExists(DataPath::Vector{String})\n\nCheck if the data pointed to by DataPath exists on disk.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.DataExists"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.ValidateDataset","page":"Library","text":"ValidateDataset(registry::DataRegistry, ID::String; allow_no_data=false)\n\nValidate Dataset ID in registry by checking that\n\nthe 'Parents' exist;\nthe 'Dataset' has an author;\nthe LastModified is after the Registered date;\nthat the DataPath and SourcePath are valid;\nthe data exists on disk \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.ValidateDataset"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.to_toml","page":"Library","text":"to_toml(x::Union{RegistryTypes, AbstractDict})\n\nConvert RegistryTypes and AbstractDict to a Dict of TOML-compatible formats.\n\n\n\n\n\nto_toml(x::Symbol)\n\nConvert Symbol to TOML-compatible String.\n\n\n\n\n\nto_toml(x::AbstractVector)\n\nConvert each element of an AbstractVector to TOML-compatible formats.\n\n\n\n\n\nto_toml(x::Union{AbstractString, Integer, AbstractFloat, Bool, Dates.DateTime, Dates.Time, Dates.Date})\n\nAllow every TOML-compatible format except AbstractDict and AbstractVector to pass unchanged.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.to_toml"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.from_toml","page":"Library","text":"from_toml(::Type{T}, x::AbstractDict) where T <: RegistryTypes\n\nConvert TOML-formatted RegistryTypes from an AbstractDict to the appropriate type.\n\n\n\n\n\nfrom_toml(::Type{Symbol}, x::AbstractString)\n\nConvert String to Symbol.\n\n\n\n\n\nfrom_toml(::Type{Vector{T}}, x::AbstractVector) where T\n\nConvert each element of a TOML-formatted AbstractVector to the appropriate type.\n\n\n\n\n\nfrom_toml(::Type{Dict{K,V}}, x::AbstractDict) where {K,V}\n\nConvert each key-value pair of a TOML-formated AbstractDict to the appropriate types.\n\n\n\n\n\nfrom_toml(::Type{Union{AbstractString, Vector{String}}}, x::Vector{String})\n\nConvert each element of a TOML-formatted Vector{String} to the appropriate type.\n\n\n\n\n\nfrom_toml(::Type{Union{AbstractString, Vector{String}}}, x::AbstractString)\n\nConvert a TOML-formatted AbstractString to the appropriate type. Special case for DataPath type requirements.\n\n\n\n\n\nfrom_toml(::Type{T}, x::T) where T <: Union{AbstractString, Integer, AbstractFloat, Bool, Dates.DateTime, Dates.Time, Dates.Date}\n\nAllow every TOML-compatible format except AbstractDict and AbstractVector to pass unchanged.\n\n\n\n\n\nfrom_toml(::Type{Any}, x)\n\nConvert an Any value to the appropriate type based on its type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.from_toml"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.SaveRegistry","page":"Library","text":"SaveRegistry(registry::DataRegistry; path::AbstractString=\"DataRegistry.toml\")\n\nSave a DataRegistry object to a TOML file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.SaveRegistry"},{"category":"function","location":"library/#DataRegistries.LoadRegistry","page":"Library","text":"LoadRegistry(filename::AbstractString)\n\nLoad a DataRegistry from a TOML file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DataRegistries.LoadRegistry"},{"category":"section","location":"#DataRegistries.jl","page":"DataRegistries.jl","text":"Documentation for DataRegistries.jl","title":"DataRegistries.jl"}]
